# Canonical author name, so that `git log`, `git shortlog -sne` and
# `git blame` agree with the byline in LICENSE and pyproject.toml.
#
# Every commit was made from one account whose git user.name was the
# GitHub handle rather than the name the project is published under.
# This maps the handle to that name on the same address; it changes what
# git displays, and rewrites nothing.
#
# Note that GitHub's web commit list does not read .mailmap -- it shows
# the account. Setting `git config user.name "Saahil Shah"` fixes future
# commits at the source; rewriting the existing history would fix the
# past, and is worth deciding before the repository is published, since
# rewriting after publication breaks every clone and fork.
Saahil Shah <saahilshah178@gmail.com> sanjaypshah210 <saahilshah178@gmail.com>
